[Event "Arrows and circles: two threats at once"]
[Site "A trap from the open games"]
[Result "0-1"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nd4 { The knight leaves e5 undefended on purpose. [%csl Ye5] } 4. Nxe5 { White takes the bait. [%cal Ge5f7] } 4... Qg5 { The queen hits the knight and the g-pawn together. [%cal Rg5e5,Rg5g2][%csl Rg2] } 5. Nxf7 { White grabs more. [%cal Gf7h8,Gf7d8] } 5... Qxg2 { Now the rook and the e-pawn hang. [%cal Rg2h1,Rg2e4] } 6. Rf1 Qxe4+ { [%cal Rd4f3][%csl Re1] } 7. Be2 Nf3# { The knight closes the net: the bishop is pinned to its own king. [%cal Re4e2,Rf3e1][%csl Re1] } 0-1

[Event "Arrows and circles: a plan"]
[Site "A Queen's Gambit, Exchange structure"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 c6 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. Qc2 O-O 9. Nge2 Re8 10. O-O Nf8 11. Rab1 { White's plan is on the queenside: push the b-pawn to b5 and break up Black's c6-d5 chain. [%cal Bb2b4,Bb4b5,Bb5c6][%csl Bc6,Bd5] } 11... Ng6 { Black looks the other way: the knight heads for the kingside. [%cal Bg6h4,Bg6f4][%csl Bh2] } 12. b4 *

