[Site "A Sicilian"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 { Three ways on for White; the circle marks the most common. [%cal Yd2d4,Yf1b5,Yc2c3][%csl Yd4] } 3. d4 (3. Bb5+ { [%cal Yc8d7,Yb8d7] } 3... Bd7) (3. c3 { [%cal Yd2d4][%csl Yd4] } 3... Nf6) 3... cxd4 4. Nxd4 { [%csl Gd4] } *

[Event "Paris"]
[Site "Paris FRA"]
[Date "1858.??.??"]
[White "Morphy, Paul"]
[Black "Duke Karl / Count Isouard"]
[Result "1-0"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 Bg4 { The bishop pins the knight against the queen. [%cal Rg4d1][%csl Rf3] } 4. dxe5 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 dxe5 6. Bc4 { Two pieces already aim at f7. [%cal Gc4f7,Gf3f7][%csl Rf7] } 6... Nf6 7. Qb3 { A double attack: b7 in front of the queen, f7 behind the bishop. [%cal Gb3b7,Gc4f7][%csl Rb7,Rf7] } 7... Qe7 8. Nc3 c6 9. Bg5 { Another pin, the knight against the queen. [%cal Rg5e7][%csl Rf6] } 9... b5 10. Nxb5 { A piece for two pawns, to keep the files open. [%cal Bb5c7,Bb5d6] } 10... cxb5 11. Bxb5+ Nbd7 12. O-O-O { Every White piece is in play; Black's king has not moved. [%cal Gd1d7,Gb5d7][%csl Rd7,Re8] } 12... Rd8 13. Rxd7 Rxd7 14. Rd1 { [%cal Gd1d7][%csl Rd7] } 14... Qe6 15. Bxd7+ Nxd7 { [%cal Gb3b8,Gd1d8] } 16. Qb8+ Nxb8 17. Rd8# { [%cal Gd8e8][%csl Re8] } 1-0
